Reason:  
The query in 1result.sql cleanly separates credits (outputs) and debits (inputs), aggregates each per concrete address and address‑type first, then joins the two aggregates to obtain a true “finalBalance = credits − debits”.  After that it derives the per‑type maximum and minimum balances.  
Because it performs the aggregation before the join it avoids duplications, counts every transaction exactly once, and requires no artificial surrogate keys; therefore its result set correctly reflects the double‑entry calculation requested.